<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project>
  <!-- Present so MSBuild does not continue searching upward and pick up the repository root
       Directory.Build.targets, which carries the Arcade and product build rules. See the reasoning
       in Directory.Build.props beside this file.

       This file is not optional once that props file exists. Isolating only the props leaves the
       root targets still applying, which imports Arcade's Sdk.targets with ArcadeSdkDir never having
       been set by Arcade's Sdk.props - measured, and it fails every asset project with:

         MSB4019: The imported project "...\Sdk\BeforeCommonTargets.targets" was not found.
                  ... "$(ArcadeSdkDir)BeforeCommonTargets.targets", which evaluated to
                  "BeforeCommonTargets.targets"

       An empty-valued property in an Import path is the diagnostic there: the import ran without the
       props file that defines the directory. -->

  <!-- Arcade defines Test, IntegrationTest and PerformanceTest as empty targets for every project it
       owns. These assets are isolated from Arcade but are still members of TestPlatform.sln, and the
       test leg runs with -projects TestPlatform.sln, so MSBuild asks every project in the solution
       for the Test target. Without these declarations the assets fail the whole test leg with:

         error MSB4057: The target "Test" does not exist in the project.

       That error is recorded in this line's own history as the reason the test leg could not be
       wired at all. It was resolved by other means before the assets were isolated; isolating them
       brings it back, so the declarations are restored here rather than by importing the root and
       undoing the isolation.

       Publish is deliberately NOT declared. Arcade lists it in its own Empty.targets because Arcade
       owns publishing for its projects; for these assets Publish is the real SDK target and
       overriding it would break them. Only the three Arcade-specific verbs belong here. -->
  <Target Name="Test" />
  <Target Name="IntegrationTest" />
  <Target Name="PerformanceTest" />
</Project>
